---
import PageLayout from "../../layouts/PageLayout.astro";

const steps = [
  { n: "01", t: "Connect", d: "Connect your prop firms and, if your plan allows, your execution providers (Tradovate, MetaApi, ProjectX). Every connection is isolated and independent.", note: "Read-only until you enable operations." },
  { n: "02", t: "Configure", d: "Register purchases, phases, entry costs and operating rules. The platform builds the accounting base of each account.", note: "No parameter decides for you: you set it." },
  { n: "03", t: "Operate", d: "On higher plans you send explicit commands from the dashboard on the prop leg, and optionally coordinate broker/slave coverage according to your parameters.", note: "Explicit command. No automated decisions, no signals." },
  { n: "04", t: "Track", d: "Operations, costs, fees, payouts and deposits all land in the same operational record, ready for reconciliation and your accountant.", note: "A single source of truth, always aligned." },
];
---
<PageLayout title="How it works" description="From prop firm management to controlled execution, in four steps." locale="en">
  <section class="bg-paper px-8 pt-32 pb-14 text-center">
    <div class="max-w-[820px] mx-auto">
      <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.3em] text-muted mb-[18px]">How it works</p>
      <h1 class="font-display font-medium tracking-[-0.01em] leading-[1.05] text-[clamp(34px,4.4vw,60px)] text-ink m-0">
        From prop firm management<br>to controlled execution.
      </h1>
      <p class="text-[19px] leading-[1.55] text-ink/70 max-w-[640px] mx-auto mt-[22px]">
        Four steps, one application. Start with the management tools and enable operations and coverage only when you need them. Control always stays with the trader.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="bg-paper px-8 pt-6 pb-24">
    <div class="max-w-[940px] mx-auto flex flex-col gap-4">
      {steps.map((s, i) => (
        <div class="grid grid-cols-[64px_1fr] md:grid-cols-[84px_1fr] gap-6 items-start bg-surface border border-border rounded-[18px] px-[30px] py-7">
          <div class:list={["font-display leading-none text-[40px]", i < 2 ? "text-positive-hover" : "text-accent"]}>{s.n}</div>
          <div>
            <h3 class="font-semibold tracking-tight text-[22px] m-0 mb-2 text-ink">{s.t}</h3>
            <p class="text-base leading-[1.55] text-ink/70 m-0 mb-3">{s.d}</p>
            <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-[13px] font-semibold text-muted bg-paper border border-border rounded-full px-3 py-[5px]">
              <span class="text-positive">✓</span>{s.note}
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="bg-ink text-paper px-8 py-[72px] text-center">
    <div class="max-w-[680px] mx-auto">
      <h2 class="font-display font-medium tracking-[-0.01em] leading-[1.05] text-[32px] text-paper m-0 mb-[18px]">The trader decides, Futugrana coordinates.</h2>
      <p class="text-base leading-[1.6] text-paper/70 m-0">
        Futugrana provides operational management and coordination software. It does not provide financial advice, trading signals or capital management. Every command starts from an explicit action of yours.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</PageLayout>
